<title>AUSTRIA: OPEC agreess quota freeze.</title>
<headline>OPEC agreess quota freeze.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC oil ministers agreed on Thursday to freeze their output quotas for six months, OPEC secretary-general Rilwanu LUkman announced.</p>
<p>The 11-nation oil cartel hopes the measure will keep prices high despite Iraq's likely resumption of exports soon under a relaxation of the U.N. Gulf War embargo against it.</p>
<p>Provision is already made for extra Iraq oil within a total output ceiling set at 25.03 million barrels daily.</p>
</text>
